<article class="env-lemma" id="0F8M">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F8M">Lemma <span data-tag="0F8M">38.42.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $D \subset X$ be an effective Cartier divisor with ideal sheaf $\mathcal{I} \subset \mathcal{O}_ X$. Let $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ be a complex of quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules such that $\mathcal{F}^ i$ is $\mathcal{I}$-torsion free for all $i$. Then $\eta _\mathcal {I}\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ is a complex of quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. Moreover, if $U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A) \subset X$ is affine open and $D \cap U = V(f)$, then $\eta _ f(\mathcal{F}^\bullet (U))$ is canonically isomorphic to $(\eta _\mathcal {I}\mathcal{F}^\bullet )(U)$. </p>
